{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Campaign shape and economy, as data so balance is a text edit rather than a rebuild.",
    "",
    "tiers is [tier1, tier2, tier3] selection weights for that night's anomalies.",
    "",
    "shift_constraints matter more than anomaly_rate: at 8-12 patients a plain 35% roll",
    "regularly produces a shift with zero anomalies (boring, and it teaches the player that",
    "ADMIT-everything works) or five in a row (feels rigged). The constraints clamp both tails.",
    "",
    "Campaign retries reroll the shift with a new seed so memorising a failed night cannot",
    "trivialise it. Endless uses a date-derived seed so everyone gets the same daily run,",
    "which is what makes a score worth sharing."
  ],
